
check-fix-commit: VIOLATION (msg.txt)
  subject:  fix: from the hook
  Gate G requires a line of the form:
    Reproduced on: <SHA / deploy URL / log excerpt / screenshot path>

  In the body. Without it, the fix is for a phantom — the user's
  symptom hasn't been observed independently before fixing began.
  Source: practices/regression-fix-protocol.md §Gate G

check-fix-commit: 1 violation(s)
Wire as commit-msg hook:  printf '#!/bin/sh\nexec rebar run check-fix-commit "$1"\n' > .git/hooks/commit-msg && chmod +x .git/hooks/commit-msg
--- exit 1 ---
